# java-gtd — agent instructions

## What this is

REST API (Spring Boot 3 + Spring AI) that classifies natural language into GTD buckets
and writes Markdown notes to an Obsidian vault. See [README.md](README.md) for the overview
and [docs/](docs/) for the API reference, architecture, and setup.

## Read first

- `README.md` — project overview and quick start
- `docs/api.md` — full endpoint reference
- `docs/architecture.md` — services, pipeline, design decisions

## Working rules

- **Never push to master directly.** Branch → push → pull request.
- Run `mvn test` before committing. All tests must pass.
- **Never put frontend code in this repo.** The frontend lives in
  [gtd-frontend](https://github.com/mmilei/gtd-frontend). Do not add anything under
  `src/main/resources/static/`.

## Key structure

```
src/main/java/.../api/        controllers (chat, buckets, undo, providers, ...)
src/main/java/.../service/    ClassifierService, VaultService, LlmProviderService, UndoStack
src/main/java/.../util/       MarkdownSerializer (YAML frontmatter)
src/main/resources/prompts/   classifier.st + classifier-fallback.st (two-level prompting)
src/test/java/                controller tests (@WebMvcTest) + VaultServiceTest (@TempDir)
```

## Local configuration

Create `src/main/resources/application-local.properties` (gitignored):

```properties
gtd.vault.path=/path/to/your/obsidian/vault
# classifier.template=custom     # to use your own gitignored prompt pair
# ollama.enabled=true            # to enable the local Ollama provider
```

Set `GROQ_API_KEY` as an environment variable. See [docs/setup.md](docs/setup.md) for all options.

